## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_leakingstreaks.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Leaking Streaks generates a layered-noise pattern resembling leaking streaks, with base and secondary layers for streaks and background stains, and a highlight layer that brightens the streaks. It can serve as a mask or building block for textures such as smudged windows or water-damaged walls.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Leaking Streaks produit des traces qui coulent et des taches de fond, avec une couche de reflets, utile en masque pour des vitres ou des murs touchés par l'eau.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude multiplies values, Center offsets them, output spans C-A to C+A; Mask Contrast increases extremeness first", "Pattern: Element Size, Offset, Tile Size as repeat period", "Primary Distortion and Primary Roughness: vertical contours and edge roughness of the base streaks", "Secondary Mask and Secondary Distortion: background horizontal folds and stains", "Tertiary Mask: visibility of the highlights", "Tertiary Balance: threshold for adding highlights, multiplied by Tertiary Mask", "Seed: randomizes the result while keeping the same look", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Values can be negative or above 1; use the Clamp options", "Complement is designed for the 0 to 1 range", "Fold has no effect when all values are positive", "Post-processing Contrast differs from Noise Contrast", "The page does not describe the algorithm, performance, or behaviour in versions other than 22.0"]

